theory.intro:
Inside a quadrant, the sign of a trigonometric ratio depends only on the quadrant the angle lies in. **ASTC** records which ratios are positive: reading anticlockwise from Q1 it spells **A**ll, **S**in, **T**an, **C**os.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2.6,0)--(2.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (0,-2.6)--(0,2.6) node[above] {$y$};
\node[font=\Large] at (1.3,1.3) {$\mathbf{A}$};
\node[font=\Large] at (-1.3,1.3) {$\mathbf{S}$};
\node[font=\Large] at (-1.3,-1.3) {$\mathbf{T}$};
\node[font=\Large] at (1.3,-1.3) {$\mathbf{C}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
ASTC identifies the positive ratios in each quadrant.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black,{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2,0)--(2,0);
\draw[black,{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (0,-2)--(0,2);
\path (2,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,2) node[above] {$y$};
\path (1,1.2) node {Q1: All} (-1,1.2) node {Q2: Sine};
\path (-1,-1.2) node {Q3: Tangent} (1,-1.2) node {Q4: Cosine};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(a) $35^{\circ}$ is in Q1, where all three ratios are positive. $\cos 35^{\circ}$ is positive.

(b) $145^{\circ}$ is in Q2, where only sine is positive. $\tan 145^{\circ}$ is negative.

(c) $235^{\circ}$ is in Q3, where only tangent is positive. $\sin 235^{\circ}$ is negative.

(d) $305^{\circ}$ is in Q4, where only cosine is positive. $\cos 305^{\circ}$ is positive.
